# point at which HttpNetworkSessionParams can still be influenced.
# MERGE: HIGH - the constructor is the ONE place this can be read, and nothing
#   in the type system enforces that. Moving this read into a setter (which
#   looks tidier) makes it compile, run, and do nothing - the profile arrives
#   after NetworkContext construction and is ignored. That was measured, not
#   assumed: instrumenting ConfigureNetworkContextParams showed the profile
#   unset for every post-hoc call. Client/test-h2-plane.js covers the ordering
